<title>BAHRAIN: Indian firms in $385mln Bahrain industry projects.</title>
<headline>Indian firms in $385mln Bahrain industry projects.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian firms are involved in three industrial projects worth $385 million in Bahrain, the Gulf Arab state's oil and industry ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In a statement it said the three industrial projects, fully managed with foreign capital, are specialised in steel and iron and would be located in the Hidd and the Aluminium Bahrain industrial areas.</p>
<p>It did not name the Indian firms.</p>
<p>The only iron plant on the island is the 4,000 tonne capacity iron pellet plant run by Gulf Industrial Investment Co.</p>
</text>
